# Day 12 - Selenium WebDriver Basics

## Objective
To understand Selenium WebDriver fundamentals, learn different locator strategies, perform web element interactions,
and automate basic web application workflows using Java.

---

## Tools Used
- Java JDK 21
- Eclipse IDE
- Selenium WebDriver
- Maven
- Google Chrome
- ChromeDriver

---

## Topics Covered

### 1. Selenium WebDriver Basics
Learned:
- Importing Selenium libraries
- Initializing WebDriver
- Opening applications using `driver.get()`
- Difference between `driver.close()` and `driver.quit()`

---

### 2. Selenium Locators
Practiced locating web elements using:
- By ID
- By Name
- By Class Name
- By Tag Name
- By Link Text
- By Partial Link Text
- By CSS Selector
- By XPath

---

### 3. Locator Strategies
Learned best practices for creating reliable locators:
- Prefer ID when available
- Use Relative XPath instead of Absolute XPath
- Use CSS Selectors for better performance where applicable
- Avoid unstable or dynamic locators

---

### 4. Web Element Actions
Practiced common Selenium methods:
- `sendKeys()`
- `click()`
- `clear()`
- `getText()`
- `getAttribute()`
- `isDisplayed()`
- `isEnabled()`
- `isSelected()`

---

### 5. Handling Web Elements
Worked with different web elements:
- Text Boxes
- Buttons
- Checkboxes
- Radio Buttons
- Dropdowns (Select Class)
- Links
- Images

---

### 6. Practice Automation Scripts
Created Selenium automation scripts for:
- Browser launch and navigation
- Login functionality
- Registration form automation
- Search functionality
- Add to Cart flow
- Locator demonstrations
- Web element interaction examples

---

## Deliverables Completed
- 10+ Selenium scripts created
- All locator types demonstrated
- Web element interaction examples completed
- Practice website automation performed
- README with Selenium WebDriver basics created

